Cheaper per-draw loops in the D3D12 command processor and render target cache: vertex buffer residency is invalidated
a 64-bit mask at a time, the used float constants are copied a run of consecutive constants per memcpy, and the stencil
tile bits are read and added in up to two contiguous runs that vectorize instead of a byte at a time with wrapping.

